Provides the ability to launch and create '*.gnr' executables.

Provides a simple desktop environment when invoked with no args.

Usages:
	gooner                                 # simple desktop environment
	gooner <executable.gnr>                # executes a *.gnr
	gooner -tell <executable.gnr>          # dumps details of a *.gnr
	gooner -make <config.xml>              # makes a *.gnr from an XML-based config

A GNR make config is written in XML, structured like this:

<gnr>
	<name>Program</name>
	<author>James FARTerson</author>
	<version>1.3.2</version>
	<elf>program.elf</elf>
</gnr>

Some notes on required tags:
	<gnr> is required as it's the root tag.
	<name> may be omitted completely and will appear empty.
	<author> may be omitted completely and will appear empty.
	<version> must follow SemVer formatting, though each digit ranges from 0-255 and will appear as 0.0.0 when omitted.
	<elf> is required and must point to a valid ELF executable relative to the XML config.

A non-standard XML implementation is used here, so comments will not work and attributes will cause tokenization errors.

Deriviation from these requirements will be caught prior to *.gnr creation and may error.
